Proposed change (not applied): a big (> 2 GiB) Data disk keeps working without a read-write store. Its writes go to RAM pages
(../PaganiPersistentData/BigVolatile.h, limit pagani-data-volatile-mib, default 1024) over the store's pages when a read-only overlay
holds them, else the seed: the fallback when the store is off/refused/failed, and the read-only verification boot (store mode 1).
Also fixes mode 1 over a resumed store for a big disk, which reached the Loader and dereferenced sparse.pages (null for big disks).
Small (<= 2 GiB) disks and the read-write direct path are unchanged.
Check: cd UniXNU-Pagani-Drivers && git apply --check drivers/PaganiPersistentData/integration/NativeRamBlock.patch

